1
00:00:05,110 --> 00:00:09,230
I met my wife in...

2
00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:13,660
It was the late 70s at Yosemite National Park.

3
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:16,430
We got a cabin in the wintertime

4
00:00:16,430 --> 00:00:18,120
and with a bunch of friends

5
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:22,040
and my little brother Wayne invited Patty

6
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:28,180
because they were friends and she was friends of his wife at the time.

7
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:30,340
And so they invited her up.

8
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:33,760
And that's the first time I met her.

9
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:38,980
And I heard that Patty said you didn't talk to her on the way back.

10
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:39,630
On the truck?

11
00:00:39,630 --> 00:00:41,260
No, we didn't have much to say.

12
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:42,300
We were both tired,

13
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:45,560
but yeah, we didn't talk too much that day.

14
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:48,860
But then when I was in back down to Concord,

15
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:53,760
we ended up going out and started dating and that.

16
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:56,260
When did you decide to get married?

17
00:00:56,260 --> 00:01:02,590
Her roommate said if I was going to hang around, I had to start paying rent or get out of the house."

18
00:01:02,590 --> 00:01:06,870
So Patty said she was gonna get out of the house.

19
00:01:06,870 --> 00:01:12,170
And then we were starting to look at renting or buying a house.

20
00:01:12,170 --> 00:01:16,250
then I told her, " Well, let's just get married, too, and get it all done."

21
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:18,430
So that's what we did.

22
00:01:18,430 --> 00:01:20,270
It doesn't sound very romantic.

23
00:01:20,270 --> 00:01:21,890
It wasn't.

24
00:01:21,890 --> 00:01:25,150
Practical, that's me, practical.

25
00:01:25,150 --> 00:01:31,220
Can you share this story when you met father-in-law at the Chinese restaurant or something?

26
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:33,340
Well, I met him at the house,

27
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:36,800
but we all went out to dinner one night.

28
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:42,340
He liked his alcohol, so he was always pretty well looped.

29
00:01:42,340 --> 00:01:48,060
And we were eating at a Szechuan Chinese place,

30
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:52,270
and he saw I had some Szechuan dish,

31
00:01:52,270 --> 00:01:55,160
and I was pushing the peppers aside.

32
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:56,680
And he goes, " What are you doing?"

33
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:58,680
I said, " Those are peppers, they're hot. "

34
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:01,320
You're not gonna eat 'em?" I said no

35
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:06,140
and he was gonna show off I guess and he grabbed one and bit into it

36
00:02:06,140 --> 00:02:08,960
he didn't like it because it was hot

37
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:14,440
and then he started drinking his drink milk water whatever was on the table

38
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:18,010
he'd never played with my food or talked about it again

39
00:02:18,010 --> 00:02:21,840
because he'd he made a mistake on that one

40
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:23,940
because those peppers are hot

41
00:02:23,940 --> 00:02:28,540
so do you have any other story with Patty's dad

42
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:30,720
Nothing that does. He comes out.

43
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:34,980
I mean, we went camping to Bucks Lake with him and her family.

44
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:37,320
And I always enjoyed being around him.

45
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:40,380
He'd always take me down to the bar here in town.

46
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:44,130
We'd come back drunk.

47
00:02:44,130 --> 00:02:48,350
I'd have four or five drinks on the counter.

48
00:02:48,350 --> 00:02:53,300
He was all done with his and I couldn't keep up with him.

49
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:54,630
Didn't even try.

50
00:02:54,630 --> 00:03:03,140
But it was... Me and Wayne Hunter and Don and everybody got taken to the bar with him.

51
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:07,320
Always had to drink too much with he and his buddies.

52
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:12,650
Do you remember when Patty met your parents the very first time?

53
00:03:12,650 --> 00:03:15,860
Um, not a specific date.

54
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:18,780
I know we invited her over.

55
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:25,310
I don't know if it was the first time or not, but one of the times in Lafayette when they still had the house there.

56
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:28,270
and we were going over for dinner.

57
00:03:28,270 --> 00:03:30,460
It was pretty early in the relationship

58
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:33,210
and she made a lemon meringue pie

59
00:03:33,210 --> 00:03:37,220
and we carried it all the way from Martinez to Lafayette

60
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:42,570
and I went around a corner and all the filling came out of the pie

61
00:03:42,570 --> 00:03:44,290
and the meringue stayed there

62
00:03:44,290 --> 00:03:47,890
so when you looked at it, it looked like a perfectly good pie

63
00:03:47,890 --> 00:03:50,940
but all the filling was on the floorboard.

64
00:03:50,940 --> 00:03:54,160
She wasn't very happy.

65
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:56,080
Well, it depends on the time of year.

66
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:59,230
In the summertime, you've got to get up early

67
00:03:59,230 --> 00:04:03,490
and do everything that you want to do before it gets too warm.

68
00:04:03,490 --> 00:04:06,780
And then in the afternoon, you sit on the porch and have a beer

69
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:09,240
and rest and listen to the creek,

70
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:11,580
take a nap or read a book.

71
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:13,410
But there's always stuff to do.

72
00:04:13,410 --> 00:04:15,860
I mean, there's always buildings to repair.

73
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:22,590
In wintertime, I'm doing a lot of fires to burn up the... stuff that's on the ground.

74
00:04:22,590 --> 00:04:26,880
So it's, there's never a dull moment. There's always something to do.

75
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:28,220
Like any house.

76
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:31,550
Maybe you can share the your latest project.

77
00:04:31,550 --> 00:04:33,520
Well, we rebuilt the stairs,

78
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:35,680
the front stairs to the house.

79
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:38,130
I've got that pretty well done.

80
00:04:38,130 --> 00:04:40,740
I hired a guy to help me on that.

81
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:47,800
We're going to have another guy come up and put new screws in the roof, in the middle roof, because they're backing out

82
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:51,620
and it's a pain so they're gonna replace them all.

83
00:04:51,620 --> 00:04:54,560
So there's there's always things that have to be done.

84
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:57,180
Well we've had every animal that

85
00:04:57,180 --> 00:05:02,270
we way back we had a porcupine right by the Wayne's house.

86
00:05:02,270 --> 00:05:05,060
We've had skunks, we got raccoons,

87
00:05:05,060 --> 00:05:07,650
we got there's a few possums,

88
00:05:07,650 --> 00:05:11,030
there's a mountain lion, there's bear.

89
00:05:11,030 --> 00:05:13,550
Patty and I saw bear here last summer.

90
00:05:13,550 --> 00:05:16,860
in the afternoon just walking through the property.

91
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:20,320
We've had coyotes, we have river otters.

92
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,940
There's just all sorts of birds,

93
00:05:22,940 --> 00:05:24,670
hawks and stuff.

94
00:05:24,670 --> 00:05:27,430
So did you see the bear in person?

95
00:05:27,430 --> 00:05:29,750
Yeah, it was in the afternoon.

96
00:05:29,750 --> 00:05:35,420
It was surprising that the last time it was a mama bear and a fairly old cub.

97
00:05:35,420 --> 00:05:40,770
And they just walked out of the woods and walked upstream

98
00:05:40,770 --> 00:05:46,250
I don't know what forced her to move during the heat of the day but something disturbed her

99
00:05:46,250 --> 00:05:51,550
so she was looking for new a new place to sit, hang out

100
00:05:51,550 --> 00:05:53,750
because it was pretty warm that day

101
00:05:53,750 --> 00:05:57,550
so you did you see the mountain lion in person too?

102
00:05:57,550 --> 00:05:59,860
yes yeah we were sitting down to dinner

103
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:01,760
it was the older bridge

104
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:04,070
and I heard this noise on the bridge

105
00:06:04,070 --> 00:06:06,710
I thought it was a dog running across the

106
00:06:06,710 --> 00:06:09,620
And I looked down about the same time it looked up

107
00:06:09,620 --> 00:06:12,770
and saw me in the window and it stopped,

108
00:06:12,770 --> 00:06:14,270
turned around and ran back.

109
00:06:14,270 --> 00:06:17,600
And it's like, wow, that was a mountain lion.

110
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:20,800
I mean, we've seen tracks and stuff.

111
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:24,670
there's been a lot of sightings in and around now.

112
00:06:24,670 --> 00:06:26,530
So they're there.

113
00:06:26,530 --> 00:06:29,120
Come up and help me. I need help.

114
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:32,800
You got a lot to learn how to take care of the place.

115
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:36,340
You've got to learn how to put it into freeze protection

116
00:06:36,340 --> 00:06:40,280
and where everything is to shut the water off if you need it.

117
00:06:40,280 --> 00:06:42,180
There's a lot to learn.

118
00:06:42,180 --> 00:06:44,000
You and Matthew need to get up

119
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:50,240
and spend some time figuring out how to put things all the way

120
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:54,520
and lock it up and what processes it needs to be done

121
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:57,920
especially the freeze drain in the house

122
00:06:57,920 --> 00:07:01,860
make sure that nothing freezes inside

123
00:07:01,860 --> 00:07:04,530
the usual stuff you do in the mountains

124
00:07:04,530 --> 00:07:07,000
yeah okay okay thank

125
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:11,800
learn how to run the backhoe!
